<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Drill 0001 — How to Use Silmulator</title>
<style>
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { transition: none !important; animation: none !important; } }

  :root {
    --bg: #0f1420;
    --surface: #1a2035;
    --surface2: #222d48;
    --surface3: #2a3860;
    --accent: #4d9fff;
    --gold: #ffc94d;
    --green: #3dd68c;
    --red: #f46a6a;
    --orange: #ff9845;
    --text: #d4daf0;
    --text-dim: #7a84a8;
    --border: #2e3a5a;
    --code-bg: #0a0f1e;
    --mono: 'Cascadia Code', 'Fira Mono', 'Consolas', monospace;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.65; min-height: 100vh; }

  /* ── Screens ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .screen { display: none; max-width: 780px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
  .screen.active { display: block; }

  /* ── Start screen ──────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .drill-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .drill-label { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.75rem; color: var(--text-dim); letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .drill-title { font-size: 2rem; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .drill-sub { color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.95rem; }

  .channel-grid { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.6rem; justify-content: center; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  .chip {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.82rem; padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; cursor: pointer;
    background: var(--surface); color: var(--text-dim); user-select: none;
    transition: border-color 0.15s, color 0.15s, background 0.15s;
  }
  .chip.active { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); background: rgba(77,159,255,.12); }
  .chip.all-chip { border-color: var(--gold); color: var(--gold); background: rgba(255,201,77,.08); }

  .start-meta { text-align: center; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.88rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }

  .shuffle-row { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.7rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-dim); }
  .toggle { position: relative; display: inline-block; width: 36px; height: 20px; }
  .toggle input { opacity: 0; width: 0; height: 0; }
  .slider {
    position: absolute; inset: 0; background: var(--surface2); border-radius: 20px; cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }
  .slider:before {
    content: ''; position: absolute; width: 14px; height: 14px; left: 3px; top: 3px;
    background: #fff; border-radius: 50%; transition: transform 0.2s;
  }
  input:checked + .slider { background: var(--accent); }
  input:checked + .slider:before { transform: translateX(16px); }

  /* ── Question screen ───────────────────────────────────────── */
  .q-header { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.8rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .q-num-badge { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--text-dim); }
  .q-progress-bar { flex: 1; height: 5px; background: var(--surface2); border-radius: 3px; min-width: 100px; }
  .q-progress-fill { height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 3px; transition: width 0.3s; }
  .q-cat-tag { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; color: var(--text-dim); }
  .q-type-tag { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem; border-radius: 12px; }
  .q-type-tag.mc      { background: rgba(77,159,255,.15); color: var(--accent); }
  .q-type-tag.written { background: rgba(255,152,69,.15); color: var(--orange); }

  .q-text { font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; line-height: 1.5; }

  pre.snippet {
    background: var(--code-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem; overflow-x: auto; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.83rem;
    line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .kw  { color: #c792ea; } .str { color: #c3e88d; } .cm  { color: #546e7a; font-style: italic; }
  .fn  { color: #82aaff; } .num { color: #f78c6c; } .cls { color: #ffcb6b; }

  /* MC */
  .options { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .options li {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 0.6rem 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; cursor: pointer; user-select: none;
    transition: border-color 0.15s, background 0.15s;
  }
  .options li:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .options li:hover:not(.locked) { border-color: var(--accent); background: rgba(77,159,255,.08); }
  .options li.correct { border-color: var(--green); background: rgba(61,214,140,.1); color: var(--green); }
  .options li.wrong   { border-color: var(--red);   background: rgba(244,106,106,.1); color: var(--red); }
  .options li.locked  { cursor: default; }
  .mc-feedback { margin-top: 0.7rem; font-size: 0.88rem; padding: 0.5rem 0.8rem; border-radius: 5px; display: none; }
  .mc-feedback.ok  { background: rgba(61,214,140,.12); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid rgba(61,214,140,.3); }
  .mc-feedback.bad { background: rgba(244,106,106,.12); color: var(--red);   border: 1px solid rgba(244,106,106,.3); }

  /* Written recall */
  textarea {
    width: 100%; min-height: 110px; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.7rem 0.9rem; color: var(--text); font-family: inherit;
    font-size: 0.93rem; resize: vertical; line-height: 1.55;
  }
  textarea:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); }
  .written-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; margin-top: 0.7rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .kw-result { margin-top: 0.8rem; font-size: 0.88rem; display: none; }
  .kw-tally { font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .kw-chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .kw-chip { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.78rem; padding: 0.2rem 0.55rem; border-radius: 12px; }
  .kw-chip.hit  { background: rgba(61,214,140,.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid rgba(61,214,140,.3); }
  .kw-chip.miss { background: rgba(244,106,106,.12); color: var(--red);   border: 1px solid rgba(244,106,106,.3); }
  .kw-note { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.8rem; margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .model-answer { display: none; margin-top: 0.8rem; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.8rem 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .model-label { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--text-dim); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
  .selfrate { display: none; margin-top: 0.7rem; display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-dim); }

  /* Nav */
  .q-nav { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }
  .q-nav-spacer { flex: 1; }

  /* Buttons */
  .btn {
    font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.85rem; padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: 5px; cursor: pointer;
    transition: opacity 0.15s, border-color 0.15s; user-select: none;
  }
  .btn:focus { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; }
  .btn-primary:hover { opacity: 0.85; }
  .btn-secondary { background: var(--surface2); color: var(--text); border-color: var(--border); }
  .btn-secondary:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .btn-green { background: var(--green); color: #000; }
  .btn-gold  { background: var(--gold);  color: #000; }
  .btn-sm    { padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem; font-size: 0.78rem; }

  /* Results */
  .result-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .score-big { font-size: 3.5rem; font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--accent); }
  .score-label { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 0.3rem; }
  .result-sections { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
  @media (max-width: 540px) { .result-sections { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .result-card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem 1.2rem; }
  .result-card h3 { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--text-dim); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
  .missed-item { background: var(--surface2); border-radius: 5px; padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem; margin-bottom: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.88rem; }
  .missed-item .mc-correct { color: var(--green); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.82rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     START SCREEN
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="screen-start" class="screen active">
  <div class="drill-header">
    <div class="drill-label">Drill 0001 · Active Recall</div>
    <div class="drill-title">How to Use Silmulator</div>
    <div class="drill-sub">20 questions · grounded in the real codebase</div>
  </div>

  <p style="text-align:center;color:var(--text-dim);margin-bottom:1rem;font-size:0.9rem;">Select the channels you want to drill, or toggle All.</p>

  <div class="channel-grid" id="channel-grid">
    <div class="chip all-chip active" data-channel="all">⚡ All channels</div>
    <div class="chip active" data-channel="workflow">Place → Connect → Drive</div>
    <div class="chip active" data-channel="code-path">SCPI code path</div>
    <div class="chip active" data-channel="sil-hil-cil">SIL / HIL / CIL</div>
    <div class="chip active" data-channel="real-code">Real code (codebase)</div>
    <div class="chip active" data-channel="bugs">Bug fixes & why</div>
  </div>

  <p class="start-meta" id="start-meta">20 questions selected</p>

  <div class="shuffle-row">
    <span>Shuffle questions</span>
    <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="shuffle-toggle" checked><span class="slider"></span></label>
  </div>

  <div style="text-align:center">
    <button class="btn btn-primary" onclick="startDrill()" style="font-size:1rem;padding:0.7rem 2rem;">Begin Drill →</button>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     QUESTION SCREEN
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="screen-question" class="screen">
  <div class="q-header">
    <span class="q-num-badge" id="q-num-badge">Q 1 / 20</span>
    <div class="q-progress-bar"><div class="q-progress-fill" id="q-progress-fill" style="width:0%"></div></div>
    <span class="q-cat-tag" id="q-cat-tag">workflow</span>
    <span class="q-type-tag mc" id="q-type-tag">MC</span>
  </div>

  <div class="q-text" id="q-text"></div>
  <pre class="snippet" id="q-snippet" style="display:none"></pre>

  <!-- MC -->
  <div id="mc-area" style="display:none">
    <ul class="options" id="mc-options"></ul>
    <div class="mc-feedback" id="mc-feedback"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- Written -->
  <div id="written-area" style="display:none">
    <textarea id="written-answer" placeholder="Type your answer here…"></textarea>
    <div class="written-actions">
      <button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" onclick="checkWritten()">Check my answer</button>
      <button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" onclick="showModel()">Show model answer</button>
    </div>
    <div class="kw-result" id="kw-result">
      <div class="kw-tally" id="kw-tally"></div>
      <div class="kw-chips" id="kw-chips"></div>
      <div class="kw-note">⚠ Keyword check is rough — judge honestly against the model answer.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="model-answer" id="model-answer">
      <div class="model-label">Model answer</div>
      <div id="model-text"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="selfrate" id="selfrate" style="display:none">
      Rate yourself:
      <button class="btn btn-green btn-sm" onclick="rateWritten('knew')">✓ Knew it</button>
      <button class="btn btn-sm" style="background:var(--red);color:#fff" onclick="rateWritten('review')">↺ Needs review</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="q-nav">
    <button class="btn btn-secondary btn-sm" id="btn-prev" onclick="prevQ()">← Prev</button>
    <div class="q-nav-spacer"></div>
    <button class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="btn-next" onclick="nextQ()">Next →</button>
    <button class="btn btn-gold btn-sm" id="btn-finish" style="display:none" onclick="showResults()">See results</button>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     RESULTS SCREEN
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div id="screen-results" class="screen">
  <div class="result-header">
    <div class="score-big" id="score-big">—</div>
    <div class="score-label" id="score-label"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="result-sections">
    <div class="result-card">
      <h3>MC misses</h3>
      <div id="mc-misses-list"><em style="color:var(--text-dim);font-size:0.88rem">None — clean sweep!</em></div>
    </div>
    <div class="result-card">
      <h3>Written — needs review</h3>
      <div id="written-review-list"><em style="color:var(--text-dim);font-size:0.88rem">None flagged.</em></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display:flex;gap:0.7rem;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:1rem;">
    <button class="btn btn-secondary" onclick="reviewMissed()">Review missed only</button>
    <button class="btn btn-primary"   onclick="location.reload()">Restart fresh</button>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// QUESTION BANK
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
const BANK = [

// ── CHANNEL: workflow ─────────────────────────────────────────────
{
  id:'w1', channel:'workflow', type:'mc',
  text:'You open Silmulator with an empty canvas. What are the three steps, in order, for a complete simulation session?',
  options:[
    { text:'Place blocks → Connect ports with wires → Drive with SCPI commands', correct:true,  why:'Correct. Every Silmulator session follows Place → Connect → Drive in that order.' },
    { text:'Send SCPI commands → Observe responses → Save the layout', correct:false, why:'Sending commands comes last, not first — there are no blocks to target yet.' },
    { text:'Connect ports → Place blocks on canvas → Load source code', correct:false, why:'You need blocks on the canvas before you can connect their ports.' },
    { text:'Open the SCPI Console → Load a layout file → Place blocks', correct:false, why:'The layout file is for restoring an existing setup; you still Place first when starting fresh.' },
  ]
},
{
  id:'w2', channel:'workflow', type:'written',
  text:'Describe two ways to add a hardware block to the canvas. (No code needed — describe the UI actions.)',
  concepts:[
    { label:'Library panel / double-click', terms:['library','double-click','double click','doubleclick'] },
    { label:'Toolbar button', terms:['toolbar','tool bar','button'] },
    { label:'Add menu', terms:['add menu','menu'] },
    { label:'Add Selected Block button', terms:['add selected','add block'] },
  ],
  model:'You can (1) double-click an instrument name in the Library panel on the left dock, (2) click the corresponding toolbar button across the top of the window, or (3) use the Add menu in the menu bar. The library panel also has an "Add Selected Block" button. All paths call the same canvas.add_block() internally.'
},
{
  id:'w3', channel:'workflow', type:'mc',
  text:'You drag from a port on a Power Supply block and release over a port on an MSP430 block. What color does the wire turn when the connection succeeds?',
  options:[
    { text:'Solid gold / yellow', correct:true,  why:'Correct. WireItem uses QPen(QColor(255, 200, 50)) — a gold/amber colour — for connected wires.' },
    { text:'Blue (same as a free port)', correct:false, why:'Blue is the idle port colour (COLOR_IDLE = QColor(100, 180, 255)). A completed wire is gold.' },
    { text:'Green (same as a connected port dot)', correct:false, why:'Green is the port dot colour when connected (COLOR_CONNECTED). The wire itself is gold.' },
    { text:'White dashed line', correct:false, why:'White dashed is the in-progress "rubber" temp wire. Once released it becomes a solid gold permanent wire.' },
  ]
},
{
  id:'w4', channel:'workflow', type:'mc',
  text:'What happens when you select a block on the canvas and type a SCPI command in the SCPI Console?',
  options:[
    { text:'The command is processed by the block\'s underlying device object, and the response is shown in the console.', correct:true,  why:'Correct. ConsolePanel._send() calls block.send_command(), which calls self.device.process(cmd).' },
    { text:'The command is broadcast to every block on the canvas simultaneously.', correct:false, why:'Broadcast requires the Simulate → "Send Broadcast Command…" menu. The console targets only selected blocks.' },
    { text:'The command is queued and only sent when you click "Run parsed commands".',  correct:false, why:'"Run parsed commands" is a Code Input block action. The console sends immediately.' },
    { text:'The command travels along the wire to the connected block.',  correct:false, why:'Wires don\'t route console commands. The console addresses the selected block directly.' },
  ]
},
{
  id:'w5', channel:'workflow', type:'written',
  text:'What is the difference between the two source-code loading modes in the Code Input block: snippet mode vs. project mode?',
  concepts:[
    { label:'Snippet: single buffer / paste', terms:['snippet','paste','single','buffer'] },
    { label:'Project: folder / tree / walk', terms:['folder','project','tree','walk','directory','rtos','firmware'] },
    { label:'Project uses CodeProject.from_path', terms:['from_path','code_project','codeproject','load_project'] },
    { label:'Both extract SCPI calls', terms:['scpi','command','extract','parse'] },
  ],
  model:'Snippet mode: you paste a single block of text directly into the editor dialog; the CodeParser processes that one buffer. Project mode: you right-click → "Load project folder…" and point at a directory root (e.g. an RTOS tree). CodeProject.from_path() walks the tree, discovers every .c/.cpp/.py file, parses each, ignores build/dist/__pycache__ dirs, and aggregates all SCPI calls. The block face switches from showing "Code: N chars" to "Project: <name>" + "Files: N/M".'
},

// ── CHANNEL: code-path ────────────────────────────────────────────
{
  id:'c1', channel:'code-path', type:'mc',
  snippet:`<span class="cm"># silmulator/gui/main_window.py — ConsolePanel</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_send</span>(self) -> None:
    cmd = self._cmd_input.toPlainText().strip()
    selected = [item <span class="kw">for</span> item <span class="kw">in</span> self.canvas.selectedItems()
                <span class="kw">if</span> isinstance(item, BaseBlock)]
    <span class="kw">for</span> block <span class="kw">in</span> selected:
        response = block.<span class="fn">send_command</span>(cmd)
        ...`,
  text:'Looking at ConsolePanel._send(): if no blocks are selected when you press Send, what happens?',
  options:[
    { text:'The method returns early after logging "No block selected on canvas"', correct:true,  why:'Correct. The list comprehension produces [], the for loop body never runs, and the method logs the no-selection message.' },
    { text:'The command is broadcast to all blocks because selected is empty', correct:false, why:'An empty list means the for-loop body never executes — no command is sent anywhere.' },
    { text:'A RuntimeError is raised because send_command requires a block', correct:false, why:'No exception — the for-loop over an empty list is a no-op.' },
    { text:'The last-used block receives the command by default', correct:false, why:'There is no "last-used block" fallback; the method guards on the selected list.' },
  ]
},
{
  id:'c2', channel:'code-path', type:'written',
  text:'Trace the complete call path from the moment a user presses Send in the SCPI Console to the moment the voltage is stored inside the Power Supply device. Name each method and file.',
  concepts:[
    { label:'ConsolePanel._send()', terms:['consolepanel','_send','console'] },
    { label:'BaseBlock.send_command()', terms:['send_command','baseblock','base_block'] },
    { label:'BaseDevice.process()', terms:['process','basedevice','base_device'] },
    { label:'ScpiParser / _handlers lookup', terms:['scpi','parser','_handlers','handler','parse'] },
    { label:'PowerSupply handler sets voltage', terms:['power_supply','voltage','channel.voltage','set_voltage'] },
  ],
  model:`1. ConsolePanel._send()  (main_window.py) — grabs the cmd string and calls block.send_command(cmd) for each selected block.
2. BaseBlock.send_command()  (base_block.py) — delegates to self.device.process(cmd); logs the (cmd, response) pair.
3. BaseDevice.process()  (base_device.py) — parses the raw string with ScpiParser, looks up self._handlers["VOLT"], calls the registered handler.
4. PowerSupply._set_voltage() / channel handler  (power_supply.py) — stores channel.voltage = 3.3 (or similar); returns "" or the new value string.
Response travels back up the chain and ConsolePanel logs it.`
},
{
  id:'c3', channel:'code-path', type:'mc',
  snippet:`<span class="cm"># silmulator/gui/blocks/code_input_block.py</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_run_commands</span>(self) -> None:
    <span class="kw">if not</span> self._parsed_commands:
        <span class="kw">return</span>
    connected_blocks = self.<span class="fn">_get_connected_blocks</span>()
    <span class="kw">for</span> parsed_cmd <span class="kw">in</span> self._parsed_commands:
        <span class="kw">for</span> block <span class="kw">in</span> connected_blocks:
            block.<span class="fn">send_command</span>(parsed_cmd.scpi_command)`,
  text:'In _run_commands(), what determines which hardware blocks receive each SCPI command?',
  options:[
    { text:'The Code Input block\'s output ports must be wired to them via _get_connected_blocks()', correct:true,  why:'Correct. _get_connected_blocks() walks self._ports, finds ports whose connected_to is not None, and returns the parent_block of each peer port. Only wired blocks receive the commands.' },
    { text:'All blocks currently on the canvas receive every command', correct:false, why:'_get_connected_blocks() only returns blocks that are wired to this Code Input block\'s ports, not every scene block.' },
    { text:'Only the block selected on the canvas receives the command', correct:false, why:'Selection state is not consulted here — connectivity (port wiring) is what matters.' },
    { text:'The command is dispatched by matching its SCPI verb to the target device type', correct:false, why:'There is no verb-to-device routing here; the same command is replayed to every connected block.' },
  ]
},
{
  id:'c4', channel:'code-path', type:'mc',
  snippet:`<span class="cm"># silmulator/devices/base_device.py</span>
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_register</span>(self, path: str, fn: Callable) -> None:
    self._handlers[path.<span class="fn">upper</span>()] = fn`,
  text:'Why does _register() uppercase the path before storing it?',
  options:[
    { text:'SCPI is case-insensitive; upper-casing normalises lookup so "volt" and "VOLT" hit the same handler', correct:true,  why:'Correct. IEEE 488.2 SCPI commands are case-insensitive. Normalising to uppercase means the parser only needs to uppercase the incoming string once and all lookups succeed.' },
